<title>JAPAN: Belgacom launches multi-currency bond--Yamaichi. [CORRECTED 08:59 GMT]</title>
<headline>Belgacom launches multi-currency bond--Yamaichi. [CORRECTED 08:59 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following multi-currency bond issue was announced by lead manager Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd on Monday:</p>
<p>BORROWER Belgacom N.V. van Publiek Recht</p>
<p>    AMT	10 billion yen</p>
<p>    COUPON   A$ 6.07 pct, marks 5.67 pct, US$ 5.87 pct</p>
<p>    MATURITY 16 Dec 2026  </p>
<p>    TYPE		Multi-currency</p>
<p>    ISS PRICE	 100.50 yen</p>
<p>    PAY DATE	  16 Dec 1996</p>
<p>    PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p>    LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA+</p>
<p>    LEAD MANAGER    Yamaichi International, Sanwa International</p>
<p>NOTES: Borrower has option of choosing the currency in which to make coupon payment.</p>
<p>(Corrects to &quot;make&quot; from &quot;receive&quot;)</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
